1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,551
Actors perform against a green screen for seamless post-production compositing.

2
00:00:04,551 --> 00:00:18,611
Chroma keying replaces the green background with any desired scene or image. Chroma key compositing, or chroma keying, is a visual-effects and post-production technique for compositing (layering) two or more images or video streams together based on colour hues (chroma range).

3
00:00:18,611 --> 00:00:23,638
Used in weather forecasts, films, and games, it allows for flexible and realistic visual effects.

4
00:00:23,638 --> 00:00:27,655
This technique makes green screens a versatile tool in modern filmmaking and broadcasting.
